        <content type="html" xml:base="https://tecnoter.io/posts/node-architecture/">&lt;h3 id=&quot;system-specifications&quot;&gt;System Specifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The tecnoter Node 1 cluster represents the pinnacle of simulated retro-computing. Built on a foundation of quartz-stable oscillators and manual beam deflection circuits, it provides unparalleled reliability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4 id=&quot;components&quot;&gt;Components:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Relay Array&lt;/strong&gt;: 1024 vacuum-sealed electromagnetic switches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Storage&lt;/strong&gt;: 50PB of mirrored holographic tape drives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cooling&lt;/strong&gt;: Liquid nitrogen sub-mersion system (Active).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This node serves as the primary gateway for all tecnoter relay communications.&lt;/p&gt;
</content>
        
